>
> Turn based game not RTS twitcher.
>
> Checking inventory does not use up a turn. Do it frequently.
>
> If you see many monsters approaching you, retreat into a corridor and
> take them on one at a time.
>
> Retreat via stairs if things are too hairy and you need to heal up.
>
> Screw conducts if these are your first few games.
>
> Low on food? Sokoban. Need gear and toys? Mines.
>
> Read the spoilers because it's not going to make the game any easier
> but it'll be decidedly less frustrating once you've read the spoilers.

Adding to that, be patient. Don't worry if you die heaps, just keep
trying.

Get used to moving diagonally. It saves time.

Keep your pet with you at all times. It's almost like having another
character with you.

Armour is almost necessary to survive. This isn't a particularly
effective strategy for experienced players, but it's worth it for you:
put on every piece of armour you find. (I'm probably going to get
yelled at for suggesting that...)

What classes do you usually play? We can help more specifically if you
tell us that.

